{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>For evermore</b> — like עולמית, for He stands forever and ever; it will be His practice forever. The master of the tradition [Masoretes] says: they are two words, and the meaning is 'until our death.' Rabbi Moses [ibn Tibbon] said: it is from the root עלם, 'He will guide us continually,' like the guidance of young women, and the meaning is as He guided us in the days of our youth. Some say: from the root of ונעלם, with good guidance hidden from the created beings."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:11.242925786Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}